# DVC ignore patterns — exclude dirs DVC should not traverse.
# See https://dvc.org/doc/user-guide/project-structure/dvcignore-files
#
# NEVER give a `!` negation a trailing slash. A trailing slash makes the pattern
# directory-only, and DVC decides directory-ness by stat-ing the working tree
# (`dvc/ignore.py`: `pattern.matches(dirname, basename, self.fs.isdir(target))`,
# then `if dir_only_pattern and not is_dir: continue`). So `!…/V0/model/` rescues
# `…/V0/model` on a machine that has pulled the data and silently stops
# rescuing it anywhere the data is absent — where the broader `…/V0/*` above it
# wins and DVC aborts with "Path … is ignored by .dvcignore:<line>". CI never
# pulls data, so every such negation was a machine-dependent gate: green
# locally, red on a fresh clone. Slash-less negations match whether or not the
# path exists, which is the only form whose meaning is the same everywhere.
# Keep the `!…/model/**` companions — they cover the contents, not the dir.

# Python bytecode — keep out of source-package directory deps so the dir hash
# tracks .py content only (jcor / simulation / _kernels are dep'd as dirs).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Legacy pipeline outputs (pre-recovery backup)
data/.pre-recovery-backup/

# Embedding content-hash resume cache
data/.emb_cache/

# Encoder vintage staircase data (t69) — verified Wikipedia inputs, existing
# corpora, and EttaX preparation/checkpoint scratch. The tokenizer and model-only
# deliverables enter DVC after training and before downstream adjudication.
data/.encoder_vintage/*
!data/.encoder_vintage/ettax

data/.encoder_vintage/ettax/*
!data/.encoder_vintage/ettax/tokenizer.json
!data/.encoder_vintage/ettax/tokenizer.json.dvc
!data/.encoder_vintage/ettax/runs

data/.encoder_vintage/ettax/runs/*
